# The raw corpus is ~35 KB per server across a few thousand servers, which is
# a couple of hundred megabytes — too big for a repo, and not ours to
# redistribute wholesale anyway.
#
# `01_collect.py` regenerates it from a public API in about twenty minutes, and
# the two files that ARE committed — analysis.json and examples.json — carry
# every figure in the post plus the real instances behind each one, so the
# numbers can be checked without re-running anything.
data/frame.jsonl
data/tools.jsonl
data/servers.jsonl
data/collect.log

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
